# 💰 Transaction Management API

A RESTful API built with Node.js, Express, and MongoDB that helps users manage their personal finances. Users can track income and expenses, monitor their balance, upload profile pictures, and view financial reports.

## 🚀 Features

* 🔐 User Authentication (Register & Login)
* 🛡 JWT Protected Routes
* 👤 User Profile Management
* 🖼 Profile Picture Upload with Cloudinary
* 💵 Income Tracking
* 💸 Expense Tracking
* 📊 Balance Calculation
* 📅 Monthly Transaction Reports
* ✏️ Update Transactions
* 🗑 Delete Transactions
* ✅ Input Validation with Zod
* 📖 Swagger API Documentation

## 🛠 Technologies Used

* Node.js
* Express.js
* MongoDB Atlas
* Mongoose
* JWT (jsonwebtoken)
* bcryptjs
* Multer
* Cloudinary
* Zod
* Swagger UI

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
src/
├── controllers/
├── middlewares/
├── models/
├── routes/
├── utils/
├── validations/
├── config/
└── server.js
```

## ⚙️ Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file:

```env
PORT=3000

MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string

JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key

CLOUDINARY_NAME=your_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_api_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_api_secret
```

Start the server:

```bash
npm run dev
```

## 🔑 Authentication

After login, include the JWT token in the Authorization header:

```text
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN
```

## 📖 API Documentation

Swagger documentation is available at:

```text
/docs
```

Example:

```text
http://localhost:3000/docs
```

or

```text
https://your-domain.com/docs
```

## 📊 Transaction Logic

* Income increases balance.
* Expenses decrease balance.
* Users cannot spend more than their available balance.
* Monthly reports provide spending and income summaries.

## 🌍 Deployment

The API can be deployed on platforms such as:

* Render
* Railway
* VPS Servers

MongoDB Atlas is used as the cloud database.

